How are the plans for other architectures?

The m68k status (which obviously can=E2=80=99t influence the release decisi=
ons)
is as follows: gcc-4.7 builds, last time I looked gcj-4.7 didn=E2=80=99t bu=
t it
is currently building again (so let=E2=80=99s see whether it does this time=
);
gcc-4.6 and gnat-4.6 are getting development and bugfixes (I=E2=80=99ve que=
ued
up some patches, but am not entirely ready with all of them, plus some
for binutils and gdb), and I=E2=80=99ve asked for help re. the gcj-4.4/gcj-=
4.6
recent problems. But nothing has tested gcj-4.7, and I fear of new and
old bugs=E2=80=A6 so I=E2=80=99d rather not switch default compiler to it a=
nytime soon.

As for gcc-4.7 in general: a friend (authoring an ObjC framework _and_
runtime) told me that it dropped support for an old method of doing
things while not fulfilling the promise to get the new method of doing
it (don=E2=80=99t exactly remember what it was, /msg js on freenode for det=
ails)
fixed, with the effect that gobjc-4.7 is virtually useless/broken.

This is hearsay, but ask him for details, and check them against
reality.

bye,
//mirabilos
